Captured output of `python -m sandbox.demo --matrix` (Phase-2 checkpoint, ADR-0002).
Each row replays a fault in a disposable container, applies an action, and asserts
recovery on app-reported metrics only. The 5 FAIL rows are expected failures: they are
the truth matrix's wrong answers, proving the sandbox rejects actions that don't work.

`after: {}` on a PASS is not a missing reading -- the fault stopped reporting its metric
entirely, i.e. it is no longer active. See sandbox/recovery.py: "absent metric = fault
inactive = 0.0", which is the strongest recovery signal available.

